         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element `Measure.group.subject[x]` has a context of Measure.group based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Measure`.\nElement `Measure.group.subject[x]` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nThe subject of the measure is critical in interpreting the criteria definitions, as the logic in the measures is evaluated with respect to a particular subject. This corresponds roughly to the notion of a Compartment in that it limits what content is available based on its relationship to the subject. In CQL, this corresponds to the context declaration." ]
